ency between the XR “click” and the neural stimulation.","position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"key":"XnblB8NCpp"}],"key":"vYlOlGWuSO"}],"key":"t8g16NWwse"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Visual-Neural Sync: The XR environment (syGlass) ensures that the visual representation of the brain matches the physical stimulation site with micrometer precision, preventing “misfires” in sensitive brain regions.","position":{"start":{"line":72,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"key":"sYqvDP5T1R"}],"key":"OL9nKKYoK1"}],"key":"m3NMXwJ211"}],"key":"Q2SeGnDfZd"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. The Nanosat Bridge (The Physical Link)","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"wjToYWPGH3"}],"identifier":"id-1-the-nanosat-bridge-the-physical-link","label":"1. The Nanosat Bridge (The Physical Link)","html_id":"id-1-the-nanosat-bridge-the-physical-link","implicit":true,"key":"N6zyyoqjOa"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modern Nanosats (3U to 12U CubeSats) act as Tactical Edge Nodes in orbit.","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"key":"Mwyg7aKdGo"}],"key":"fcjhWhBCoh"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Hardware: The Nanosat carries a Q-NET-compatible laser terminal or a high-frequency Ka-band radio.","position":{"start":{"line":76,"column":1},"end":{"line":76,"column":1}},"key":"bnGQXThl32"}],"key":"Mxdx1m2SPj"}],"key":"rh4VDIndPr"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Link: The MEG-fiber interface (worn by the user) transmits data to a local ground terminal (running your K3s/Go/Envoy stack). This terminal “uplinks” the encrypted neural stream to the Nanosat.","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"jk5Mq4OOmb"}],"key":"oiv02o733s"}],"key":"XcsWJljEGN"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Q-NET Extension: Some Nanosats now perform Space-to-Ground Quantum Key Distribution (QKD). The satellite beams entangled photons down to the ground terminal, providing the “Quantum Seed” for your TLS 1.3 tunnel even in areas without physical fiber.","position":{"start":{"line":78,"column":1},"end":{"line":78,"column":1}},"key":"rLm6rjtwJi"}],"key":"AAnul0eyTL"}],"key":"pAQMoIHKMu"}],"key":"txvEfHMgzL"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. CSDAP Integration (The Data Layer)","position":{"start":{"line":80,"column":1},"end":{"line":80,"column":1}},"key":"yXnFVz2Giq"}],"identifier":"id-2-csdap-integration-the-data-layer","label":"2. CSDAP Integration (The Data Layer)","html_id":"id-2-csdap-integration-the-data-layer","implicit":true,"key":"Bj7V6Avrxd"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"CSDAP is the NASA/DoD program that buys commercial satellite data (from companies like Planet, Spire, or BlackSky) for government use.","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"DnzbTPo2u9"}],"key":"TS4ou87Et8"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contextual Awareness: CSDAP provides high-resolution imagery and RF signals from the user’s specific location.","position":{"start":{"line":82,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"key":"ZwT91kMEYu"}],"key":"eDe1J67aFj"}],"key":"tZyuLSE0ca"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Fusion: Your Go-based microservice in the cloud merges the “Neural Stream” (what the user is thinking/feeling) with “CSDAP Data” (what the satellites see around the user).","position":{"start":{"line":83,"column":1},"end":{"line":83,"column":1}},"key":"JyyxMf8CYK"}],"key":"st8Z7fY3hB"}],"key":"uIkyZcL4qi"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: If the user’s neural interface detects a high-stress “threat” response, the system automatically pulls the latest CSDAP SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) imagery of the surrounding 5km to identify potential hazards.","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"key":"Lummy8P0oB"}],"key":"KmYEo0csap"}],"key":"wIuGIyffwY"}],"key":"kibqi5tT4C"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":86,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Implementing the “Space-Aware” Pod","position":{"start":{"line":86,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"key":"p1wDSnzI5W"}],"identifier":"id-3-implementing-the-space-aware-pod","label":"3. Implementing the “Space-Aware” Pod","html_id":"id-3-implementing-the-space-aware-pod","implicit":true,"key":"WisaZ7Eqsj"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To make this work, your K3s Pods must be “Space-Aware”:\nProtocol Optimization: Standard TCP/IP fails over satellite due to high latency. Your Envoy Wrapper is configured to use QUIC (UDP-based) or SCPS (Space Communications Protocol Specifications) to keep the neural stream fluid.","position":{"start":{"line":87,"column":1},"end":{"line":87,"column":1}},"key":"OdGAJ1e4TG"}],"key":"ps4lyWsvtF"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Intermittent Connectivity: The Go driver uses a “Store and Forward” buffer. If the Nanosat passes behind a mountain, the MEG-powered interface stores the neural data in a local Sidecar and bursts it to the satellite once the link is restored.","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"key":"rLZ304NA8q"}],"key":"gv4egvmRaO"}],"key":"DgsZx5hD15"}],"key":"oc6wxNGOE5"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Identity & Access (Entra ID in Space)","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"S6Qjv9vDmm"}],"identifier":"id-4-identity-access-entra-id-in-space","label":"4. Identity & Access (Entra ID in Space)","html_id":"id-4-identity-access-entra-id-in-space","implicit":true,"key":"hvhTJI9cuz"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cross-Domain Identity: Entra ID manages the permissions for the satellite uplink. The Nanosat verifies the user’s Workload Identity before allowing the data to enter the “Space Segment” of the DoDIN.","position":{"start":{"line":92,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"key":"uO59rvMvkc"}],"key":"bZjzoeroTA"}],"key":"kd1IGL3qvg"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream Access: A commander at a HQ can view the “CSDAP + Neural” fusion dashboard. Think Neuralink with first person visual and subtitles. They authenticate via Entra ID MFA, and the Envoy Proxy decrypts the satellite-delivered stream in real-time.","position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"key":"oXp4wd8J6U"}],"key":"VYv7xCJ1CL"}],"key":"LuiiYS6Sju"}],"key":"UPVPqQb3Dy"}],"key":"hHFT9QDtng"}],"key":"SghhOuiihS"},"references":{"cite":{"order":["Chung_2022"],"data":{"Chung_2022":{"label":"Chung_2022","enumerator":"1","doi":"10.1145/3502181.3531475","html":"Chung, J., Zacherek, W., Wisniewski, A., Liu, Z., Bicer, T., Kettimuthu, R., & Foster, I. (2022). SciStream: Architecture and Toolkit for Data Streaming between Federated Science Instruments. <i>Proceedings of the 31st International Symposium on High-Performance Parallel and Distributed Computing</i>, 185–198. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3502181.3531475\">10.1145/3502181.3531475</a>","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3502181.3531475"}}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Index","url":"/index-12","group":"Dashboard"},"next":{"title":"Biological Assets","url":"/bio-assets","group":"Dashboard"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}